# Act 2 — the session that outlives its runtime. Task 6.2.
#
# Every line below runs AFTER the hosted runtime has been killed with SIGKILL, and the editor does
# not know it yet: session.py holds this act at a Unix FIFO until the kill has happened, so the
# ordering is decided rather than raced. What the act asserts is not that these commands are clever
# — it is that they all still work, that the loss is surfaced with something to act on, and that the
# document ends the act intact and unsaved.
scene.create-entity
scene.create-entity
edit.undo
edit.redo
scene.create-entity
edit.undo
